      "writtenOn": "2020-11-24T18:55:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you just want to know what the wall time for the mutator is the easiest way is to add a printf in runMutator in build/blueprint/context.go.  If you would like more detail you can enable CPU profiling, but it\u0027s a little tricky.  Run `m nothing` to make sure soong_build is built, and then run:\n\n ANDROID_JAVA_HOME\u003dprebuilts/jdk/jdk11/linux-x86 ANDROID_JAVA8_HOME\u003dprebuilts/jdk/jdk8/linux-x86 out/soong/.bootstrap/bin/soong_build -t -l out/.module_paths/Android.bp.list -b out/soong -n out -d out/soong/build.ninja.d -globFile out/soong/.bootstrap/build-globs.ninja -o out/soong/build.ninja -cpuprofile\u003d/tmp/soong_build.pprof Android.bp\n\nThe samples from individual mutators are labeled using Go\u0027s \"profiler labels\", and you can filter them in the `go tool pprof` tool.",
      "parentUuid": "60fcbbf0_6b9c99a5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 92,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 92,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "9035ca756d1b64c52f4f1efb9bdc66a872426f1f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "08f784b0_0f8e157e",
        "filename": "cc/cc.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 92,
      "author": {
        "id": 1337669
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-11-25T06:36:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks, that\u0027s very useful.\n\n- `go tool pprof -tags -tagfocus sabi_deps out/soong/.bootstrap/bin/soong_build /tmp/soong_build.pprof`\nThe pprof collected results aren\u0027t very helpful in my case here. The collected profile is inconsistent across runs, and the parallel and non-parallel runs yield similar profile results. This is probably due to sabiDepsMutator being a short-lived mutator, and the probe-based profiler doesn\u0027t have enough time to collect sufficient samples.\n\n- Print mutator run time (wall time) in `runMutators()` in blueprint/context.go.\nUsing this method I found that *non-parallel* sabiDepsMutator run consistently better than parallel.\nParallel sabiDepsMutator spends ~290ms, and non-parallel spends ~190ms (AOSP). I can get a similar result in internal.\nA surprising result, but also kind of expected. Since sabiDepsMutator is short-lived, it kind of makes sense that the parallel speed up is smaller than the overhead to manage a parallel runtime.\n\nI\u0027ll leave this as-is and not make sabi_deps parallel.",
      "parentUuid": "14c155db_31c2ad22",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 92,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 92,
        "endChar": 42
      },
